  data: {
    LLM: "Hearts is permanent trump. Each player bids once (minimum 1 trick); the sum of all bid values must be at least 11 or hands are thrown in and the next player deals. Player to dealer's right leads; play is anticlockwise. Follow suit if possible; otherwise play any card. Highest trump or highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Bids 1–6 score face value if made, 7+ score double; failing scores minus the bid value.",
    Player: "Hearts is permanent trump. Each player bids once (minimum 1 trick); the sum of all bid values must be at least 11 or hands are thrown in and the next player deals. Player to dealer's right leads; play is anticlockwise. Follow suit if possible; otherwise play any card. Highest trump or highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Bids 1–6 score face value if made, 7+ score double; failing scores minus the bid value.",
    objective: "The partnership wins when one partner's score reaches or exceeds 41 points and the other partner's score is positive. If both partnerships reach this in the same deal, the one with the higher total wins.",
